scratchpad

# RUNTIME DATA — never part of an image.
#
# These are bind-mounted at runtime (see docker-compose.yml), so shipping them
# is pure waste, and on a real deployment it is dangerous waste: the source
# cache is budgeted at 2 TB. `docker build` sends the whole context to the
# daemon before the first instruction runs, so a populated cache/ or media/
# would push hundreds of gigabytes across and can wedge the box.
#
# Seen for real: transcode/ held 98 MB of leftover HLS segments and was 98% of
# a 102 MB build context.
cache/
media/
data/
transcode/

# Tizen build output (regenerate with `npm run tv-build`). public/tv-build IS
# needed in the image — it's the Chromium-69 bundle old Samsung TVs load — but
# the packaging artifacts around it are not.
tizen/Mediawan/Debug/
tizen/Mediawan/Release/
tizen/Mediawan/.buildResult/
*.wgt
